---

# Show Image on E-Paper

Use this skill when the user asks to show, display, or preview an image, photo,
or picture on the e-paper (e-ink) display. The panel is 184x384 with 4 colors
(black / white / yellow / red).

The image is scaled down to fit inside the panel (never enlarged) and centered
by default. Colors are quantized with Floyd-Steinberg dithering; small images
keep their original size, centered.

Run exactly one script with `lua_run_script`.

If `lua_run_script` returns an error, report that error directly to the user.
Do not retry with changed arguments in the same turn unless the user explicitly asks.

## Script Args Schema

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "path": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Path to a readable .jpg file. Demo images: {CUR_SKILL_DIR}/assets/demo_landscape.jpg (640x480), {CUR_SKILL_DIR}/assets/demo_portrait.jpg (tall), {CUR_SKILL_DIR}/assets/demo_small.jpg (96x96, shown at original size)."
    },
    "dither": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "default": true,
      "description": "Floyd-Steinberg dithering. Keep true for photos; set false for crisp line art or black-and-white text screenshots."
    },
    "background": {
      "type": "integer",
      "enum": [0, 1, 2, 3],
      "default": 1,
      "description": "Background fill around the image: 0 black, 1 white, 2 yellow, 3 red."
    },
    "x": {
      "type": "integer",
      "description": "Left edge of the image in pixels (0..183). Omit to center horizontally."
    },
    "y": {
      "type": "integer",
      "description": "Top edge of the image in pixels (0..383). Omit to center vertically."
    }
  },
  "required": ["path"]
}
```

## Tool Call Inputs

Show the landscape demo image:

```json
{"path":"{CUR_SKILL_DIR}/scripts/show_image.lua","args":{"path":"{CUR_SKILL_DIR}/assets/demo_landscape.jpg"}}
```

Show a line-art image without dithering:

```json
{"path":"{CUR_SKILL_DIR}/scripts/show_image.lua","args":{"path":"/path/to/diagram.jpg","dither":false}}
```

## Recommended Flow

1. Pick the image path: from the conversation, a storage path the user names, or one of the demo assets above.
2. Run `{CUR_SKILL_DIR}/scripts/show_image.lua` with that path (and `dither` if the image is line art).
3. Report the outcome: the scaled size and position. A full refresh takes several seconds; colors are reduced to black / white / yellow / red.
